    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** leading the charge, boasting an elite 77.46 score. His matchup against Kumar Rocker is optimal; between his plus-platoon advantage and a favorable spot in the order, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary engine for SB production, which remains our highest priority category. **James Wood** also demands attention at 72.41, bolstered by a strong 0.415 xwOBA and a prime leadoff opportunity against Ure\u00f1a. Meanwhile, **Trevor Story** continues to look like a high-upside play at 68.70, as he benefits from a generous 4.58 xERA matchup that allows him to exploit the park factors effectively.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer today was bypassing **Max Muncy** on the bench. With a score of 49.03, he remained a legitimate contender for the UTIL slot, but he ultimately lost out to the superior platoon splits and park-adjusted outlook of **Josh Naylor** (62.46). While **Max Muncy** offers power, his negative SP skill adjustment against Bryan Woo neutralized his base projection. Elsewhere, the lower end of the lineup is tighter; **Griffin Conine** barely cleared our 40.0 threshold at 40.08, narrowly escaping the bench despite facing an elite arm in Tyler Glasnow. His inclusion is purely situational, predicated on the desperate need for his specific power profile to keep our pace in HR and RBI.\n\nRisk management remains critical as we navigate several \"Lineup Pending\" tags for players like **Gabriel Moreno**, **Cole Young**, **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Josh Naylor**. Any defensive replacements or late-scratches could shift these scores significantly. Furthermore, we are keeping a close eye on **Griffin Conine**; should he be shifted down the lineup or if weather delays materialize, we are prepared to pivot, though we have little confidence in the current bench depth\u2014including **Isaac Paredes** and **Travis Bazzana**\u2014to provide a higher floor given their respective matchups against Seymour and Prielipp. For today, we lean into our speed-first strategy with **Corbin Carroll** and **Brice Turang** anchoring the top of the card.",
